@startuml phase0-loopback
title Phase 0 — end-to-end loopback\nENG publishes SyncSegments to a live ISBM provider and reads it back

skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 240
skinparam ParticipantPadding 10
skinparam BoxPadding 12

actor "Operator" as User

box "SimHost"
  participant "ENG\npersonality" as Eng
  participant "Outbox\ndispatcher" as Outbox
  participant "Inbox\npump" as Inbox
  participant "Session\nmanager" as Sessions
end box

database "Azure SQL\nschema: eng" as Db
database "Blob\nsandbox-payloads" as Blob
participant "ws-ISBM provider" as Isbm

== One-time setup ==

User -> Eng : POST /admin/schema/init
activate Eng
Eng -> Db : create tables from the EF model
note right of Eng
  No migrations. The schema name is a
  parameter, and every session starts
  from reset — there is nothing to
  migrate and no history worth keeping.
end note
Eng --> User : 10 tables in schema eng
deactivate Eng

User -> Isbm : POST /admin/isbm/channels/ensure
activate Isbm
Isbm --> User : channel /OIIE-SANDBOX/Enterprise/Site/Eng
deactivate Isbm

== Authoring — no messages ==

User -> Eng : POST /admin/eng/tags\nTIC-106
activate Eng
Eng -> Db : INSERT Tag, Provenance\n(one transaction)
note right of Eng
  ENG's own vocabulary: TagNumber,
  ServiceDescription, PidReference.
  Nothing here is a Segment.
end note
Eng --> User : WorkInProgress
deactivate Eng

== Release event ==

User -> Eng : POST /admin/eng/promote\n"Rev C — Unit 101 reroute"
activate Eng

Eng -> Eng : validation gate

alt findings present
  Eng -> Db : INSERT ValidationFinding
  Eng --> User : 422 with findings — release blocked
else gate passes
  Eng -> Db : UPDATE Tag → Published\nINSERT NamedVersion, Outbox\n(single transaction)
  note right of Eng
    Publication intent commits with the
    domain change, so the BOD is derived
    from persisted state. A form never
    authors a BOD.
  end note
  Eng --> User : released
end
deactivate Eng

== Dispatch ==

Outbox -> Db : SELECT Outbox WHERE Pending
activate Outbox

Outbox -> Outbox : SyncSegmentsBuilder\nTag rows → Segment + attributes
note right of Outbox
  The mapper is the interoperability
  work: ENG column names on one side,
  CCOM elements on the other.
end note

Outbox -> Sessions : session for Publication
activate Sessions
Sessions -> Db : SELECT IsbmSession
alt no stored session
  Sessions -> Isbm : POST publication-sessions\n{channelUri}
  activate Isbm
  Isbm --> Sessions : sessionId
  deactivate Isbm
  Sessions -> Sessions : confirm before use
  note right of Sessions
    Session state is eventually
    consistent; a post issued straight
    after open can fail against a
    session not yet visible.
  end note
  Sessions -> Db : INSERT IsbmSession
end
Sessions --> Outbox : sessionId
deactivate Sessions

Outbox -> Isbm : POST sessions/{id}/publications\nmessageContent{mediaType, inlineContent}
activate Isbm
Isbm --> Outbox : messageId
deactivate Isbm

Outbox -> Blob : store BOD body
Outbox -> Db : INSERT Message (Outbound)\nUPDATE Outbox → Posted
deactivate Outbox

== Delivery ==

Inbox -> Sessions : session for Subscription
activate Inbox
activate Sessions
Sessions -> Isbm : POST subscription-sessions\n{channelUri, topics, filterExpressions}
note right of Sessions
  filterExpressions must be present.
  Absent leaves it null rather than
  empty, and the provider's filter
  engine has no null guard.
end note
Sessions --> Inbox : sessionId
deactivate Sessions

Inbox -> Isbm : GET sessions/{id}/publication
activate Isbm
Isbm --> Inbox : messageId, inlineContent
deactivate Isbm

Inbox -> Db : SELECT cursor
alt already handled
  Inbox -> Isbm : DELETE sessions/{id}/publication
  note right of Inbox
    Read but not removed on an earlier
    run. Removing rather than
    reprocessing is what stops a restart
    duplicating work.
  end note
else new message
  Inbox -> Inbox : BodEnvelope.Parse\nvalidate against XSDs
  Inbox -> Blob : store BOD body
  Inbox -> Db : INSERT Message (Inbound)

  alt handler registered
    Inbox -> Inbox : bind classes, ingest properties
    Inbox -> Db : UPDATE Message → Applied
  else no handler
    Inbox -> Db : UPDATE Message → Pending
    note right of Inbox
      Archived, not dropped. A participant
      is expected to receive BODs it
      cannot act on, and the wire view has
      to show them.
    end note
  end

  Inbox -> Db : UPDATE cursor
  Inbox -> Isbm : DELETE sessions/{id}/publication
end
deactivate Inbox

== Result ==

User -> Eng : GET /admin/eng/messages
activate Eng
Eng --> User : two rows, one correlationId\nOutbound then Inbound
deactivate Eng

note over User, Isbm
  The correlation id travels in ApplicationArea/BODID, so it survives the
  store-and-forward hop that HTTP tracing cannot. One query reconstructs the
  exchange across every participant and both providers.
end note

@enduml
